From: BOB LECHEVALIER
Subj: TO LEARN LOJBAN

The SA article is very much lacking, which is why no one ever learned
the language.  I'd hoped that some of the material in JL was being
helpful to people, but I have not been emphasizing the grammar except
to teach it by example.  We will be putting more of the grammar in the
later issues of JL.

I can't say the price of the teaching package, and it will depend on
whether you use Logflash or flashcards to learn the vocabulary, et. al.
The first time around it will be more expensive due to the limited
production runs, which is unfortunate.  But our finances don't allow
us to over order.

I've been trying to reach you Thomas, re the class.  But my phone# for
you seems to be invalid.  The class will start 29 January at my place
near the Vienna Metro station, and run from 7PM-1015PM, or thereabouts.
Call me sometime if I can't reach you at work before you see this.
(703-385-0273).

